  "notes": "Built from homeassistant/components/met_eireann/weather.py and the PyMetEireann 2024.11.0 library it calls. Core's met_eireann snapshot comes from a stub whose forecast entries carry only condition, datetime and temperature, and whose state is not snapshotted, so it says nothing about the real shape. Values are realistic for Dublin (Europe/Dublin, UTC+0 in November). Current: never apparent_temperature, dew_point, uv_index, visibility or ozone; wind_gust_speed only when the API gives windGust, cloud_coverage only when it gives cloudiness (a one-decimal float). wind_bearing is degrees as a one-decimal float (core's test stub uses the string 'NE', the library never does). Condition: Met Éireann symbol ids mapped by CONDITION_MAP; an id it does not list passes through unchanged, e.g. 'Dark_LightRainThunderSun' (the map lists 'LightRainThunderSun' twice instead), and 'sunny' is matched by substring of 'Sun'. Hourly: exactly 24 entries, the next 24 whole hours (now + 1 h onward), datetimes in UTC; symbol and precipitation come from the interval ending at that hour; never precipitation_probability, templow, dew_point or uv_index. Daily: 5 entries starting tomorrow (today is never included), each stamped 12:00 local time in UTC; temperature/templow are the max/min of that day's points from noon to midnight only, so templow is an evening value, not the overnight low; precipitation sums every precipitation interval from noon on that starts or ends on that day; condition, pressure, humidity and wind_bearing come from the step nearest noon; never cloud_coverage or precipitation_probability. Any forecast key whose value is None is dropped. No changes were needed for realism.",
